WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:11.790
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:01.940 --> 00:02.780
Whoa!

00:07.190 --> 00:08.920
This is Eisetsu City.

00:09.580 --> 00:12.520
For Satoshi, it is the city where his last badge is.

00:13.410 --> 00:15.490
We've finally come to Eisetsu City!

00:16.070 --> 00:17.550
It's snow! Snow!

00:20.110 --> 00:20.620
Yay!

00:21.040 --> 00:22.550
Eureka, you are going to catch a cold!

00:22.890 --> 00:24.430
Don't worry!

00:24.950 --> 00:27.040
Satoshi, it's finally time for your eighth.

00:27.040 --> 00:27.660
Do your best!

00:27.910 --> 00:28.340
I will.

00:28.800 --> 00:30.780
I'll make sure to get it and catch up to Shota!

00:31.040 --> 00:32.840
I will root for you to the best of my ability.

00:33.290 --> 00:35.500
I wonder if we'll get to see Satoshi Gekkouga today.

00:36.000 --> 00:37.340
"Satoshi Gekkouga"?

00:37.590 --> 00:38.770
What is that?

00:39.140 --> 00:42.670
I gave Gekkouga's new form a name!

00:43.000 --> 00:44.560
Oh, nice one!

00:44.560 --> 00:45.850
After all, it looks a lot like Satoshi, right?

00:46.190 --> 00:46.750
Yeah!

00:46.750 --> 00:49.040
That name is just a description.

00:49.040 --> 00:49.570
It's fine!

00:50.650 --> 00:53.200
All right, let's set off towards the Eisetsu Gym!

00:53.560 --> 00:55.430
I'll get my final badge!

01:05.530 --> 01:07.060
That seems to be the Eisetsu Gym.

01:07.430 --> 01:08.870
Let's race there, then!

01:09.120 --> 01:10.610
All right, ready... Go!

01:10.610 --> 01:11.760
Hey, no fair!

01:11.760 --> 01:14.330
We should walk slowly when on snow!

01:14.800 --> 01:16.630
Shota, please watch us.

01:17.200 --> 01:18.850
I want to get my eighth badge...

01:19.440 --> 01:21.080
...and fight you at the League, no matter what.

01:21.690 --> 01:23.350
I can't leave it at that loss.

01:24.860 --> 01:26.350
Let's settle this at the League!

01:29.040 --> 01:30.760
Yes, of course!

01:31.770 --> 01:33.350
Satoshi, Shota!

01:34.000 --> 01:36.010
Hurry up, or we're going to go on ahead!

01:36.340 --> 01:37.740
Hurry, hurry!

01:38.890 --> 01:39.460
Let's go!

01:39.770 --> 01:40.120
Okay!

01:48.370 --> 01:54.080
Eisetsu Gym Match!
A Battlefield of Ice!!

01:55.020 --> 02:04.920
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:55.020 --> 02:04.920
Z

02:02.750 --> 02:03.430
Excuse me.

02:03.840 --> 02:04.760
I'd like to have a Gym match.

02:11.160 --> 02:13.170
Oh, they're Pokémon!

02:16.310 --> 02:18.080
Kachikohru, the Ice Chunk Pokémon.

02:18.620 --> 02:23.730
It blocks opponents with the ice that shields its body. It uses cold air to repair any cracks with new ice.

02:24.150 --> 02:25.180
Wow.

02:25.180 --> 02:26.430
Are they here to pick us up?

02:28.880 --> 02:30.320
Welcome to the Eisetsu Gym.

02:30.970 --> 02:35.830
It's very cold inside. Please protect yourself against the cold before entering.

02:36.300 --> 02:38.120
So even the interior of the Gym is cold.

02:38.530 --> 02:41.410
Good thing we borrowed these at the Pokémon Center!

02:42.040 --> 02:43.630
We're all prepared here.

02:44.150 --> 02:45.880
Please come in, then.

02:49.930 --> 02:51.100
Whoa!

03:04.230 --> 03:05.760
You guys did... Well, you know?

03:06.270 --> 03:07.360
Good job making it here.

03:08.820 --> 03:10.360
I request a Gym match.

03:10.910 --> 03:11.250
Hm.

03:11.750 --> 03:12.870
I'm Urup.

03:13.310 --> 03:16.370
I'm... You know. The Gym Leader of the Eisetsu Gym!

03:16.900 --> 03:19.620
Isn't it cold, sitting on top of ice like that?

03:21.410 --> 03:26.210
Well, you know... When you're like me, you feel that ice has a heart as warm as anyone!

03:26.670 --> 03:28.630
This temperature is just right for me.

03:29.360 --> 03:29.590
Huh?

03:30.230 --> 03:31.820
Weren't you here the other day...?

03:32.720 --> 03:33.040
Yes.

03:34.170 --> 03:36.100
Thank you for bearing with me on that occasion.

03:36.700 --> 03:37.780
That battle was...

03:38.100 --> 03:39.600
Yeah, it was heated.

03:40.970 --> 03:42.170
Thank you very much!

03:43.540 --> 03:45.190
So who's the challenger?

03:45.600 --> 03:48.170
It's me. My name is Satoshi and I come from Masara Town.

03:50.230 --> 03:50.810
How many badges?

03:51.350 --> 03:52.160
Seven!

03:52.620 --> 03:53.380
I see.

03:54.030 --> 03:56.440
So your final badge depends on this Gym match.

03:57.620 --> 03:58.580
Make sure to enjoy it!

03:59.110 --> 03:59.660
I will!

04:00.960 --> 04:02.350
Serena, please hold this for me.

04:04.460 --> 04:05.810
I'm starting to get fired up!

04:11.330 --> 04:14.720
All right, the Gym match of the Eisetsu Gym will now begin!

04:15.350 --> 04:17.730
Both may use three Pokémon each.

04:17.990 --> 04:21.800
The battle is concluded as soon as one party's Pokémon are all unable to battle.

04:22.550 --> 04:27.340
Furthermore, only the challenger is allowed to substitute his Pokémon during the battle.

04:28.210 --> 04:30.670
Y'know what? Ice is both extremely hard...

04:31.390 --> 04:32.740
...and terribly fragile at the same time.

04:33.740 --> 04:40.750
You know what that means? Depending on which Pokémon you choose and what moves they use, my strength changes as well.

04:41.880 --> 04:43.590
But that's how it should be.

04:44.690 --> 04:46.190
Anyway, enough of my rambling!

04:46.920 --> 04:49.210
Let's get this show on the road!

04:49.770 --> 04:49.960
Okay!

04:50.660 --> 04:52.400
Luchabull, I choose you!

04:56.960 --> 04:59.820
Be careful. Today, your ring is an ice field.

05:01.270 --> 05:02.770
Come out, Yukinooh!

05:14.530 --> 05:15.110
Hail?

05:15.650 --> 05:16.650
This is troublesome.

05:21.980 --> 05:24.660
It's... You know. Yukinooh's Ability.

05:25.090 --> 05:29.290
Yukinooh can turn the weather on the field into a hailstorm.

05:30.110 --> 05:32.300
The hail will deal damage.

05:32.490 --> 05:33.170
What?

05:33.670 --> 05:34.820
Bring it on.

05:35.270 --> 05:37.660
Luchabull, let's use all we've got right from the start!

05:38.710 --> 05:39.760
Flying Press!

05:49.180 --> 05:51.390
Oh, it's got vigour.

05:54.720 --> 05:55.830
The damage it's taken from the hail is...!

05:56.400 --> 05:57.280
High Jump Kick!

06:00.200 --> 06:00.520
Hmph...

06:01.460 --> 06:02.530
Ice Shard!

06:12.760 --> 06:13.890
Wood Hammer!

06:19.350 --> 06:20.680
Dodge and use Flying Press!

06:31.680 --> 06:32.470
We're not done yet.

06:32.670 --> 06:33.430
High Jump Kick!

06:42.940 --> 06:43.670
What?!

06:52.910 --> 06:55.880
Yukinooh is unable to battle! Luchabull wins!

06:56.740 --> 06:57.830
Good job, Luchabull!

06:59.260 --> 07:00.070
All right!

07:00.070 --> 07:01.770
Luchabull is so cool!

07:02.340 --> 07:04.000
That was a swift attack, just as you would expect from Satoshi.

07:04.330 --> 07:05.590
He is pumped.

07:05.840 --> 07:07.300
It's his last badge, after all.

07:10.730 --> 07:12.620
Yukinooh, thanks for the hard work.

07:13.860 --> 07:15.440
Luchabull, we'll continue like this!

07:18.360 --> 07:19.160
Your turn.

07:25.060 --> 07:26.550
Let's go, Crebase!

07:31.770 --> 07:32.320
It's huge...

07:36.020 --> 07:39.160
Crebase, the Iceberg Pokémon. The evolved form of Kachikohru.

07:39.860 --> 07:46.200
Its ice-covered body is as hard as steel. Its cumbersome frame crushes anything that stands in its way.

07:47.080 --> 07:47.990
Let's finish this in one go!

07:48.380 --> 07:49.400
Use Karate Chop!

07:50.750 --> 07:51.880
Stone Edge!

08:07.670 --> 08:09.560
Its Ability is Ice Body.

08:10.030 --> 08:14.730
That means...  You know. While it's hailing, it recovers stamina little by little.

08:15.260 --> 08:15.870
Recover?

08:17.030 --> 08:20.110
I see. That's why he sent out Yukinooh first.

08:20.440 --> 08:20.970
We're not done yet!

08:21.260 --> 08:22.110
High Jump Kick!

08:25.410 --> 08:26.430
Gyro Ball!

08:33.270 --> 08:33.920
It got repelled!

08:37.030 --> 08:38.560
It's not over yet. Flying Press!

08:47.750 --> 08:48.430
Luchabull!

08:53.150 --> 08:56.470
Luchabull is unable to battle! Therefore, Crebase wins!

08:56.790 --> 08:57.870
No way...

08:58.280 --> 08:59.610
The hail is quite effective.

09:00.020 --> 09:01.660
But still, it's one-to-one.

09:02.010 --> 09:02.780
They are even.

09:04.640 --> 09:06.460
Well done, Luchabull.

09:14.470 --> 09:15.590
You're next, Fiarrow!

09:17.130 --> 09:18.110
I'm counting on you!

09:22.410 --> 09:24.420
Fiarrow, don't let the hail bother you.

09:24.790 --> 09:25.870
Let's not give them time to rest!

09:26.870 --> 09:28.160
Flame Charge!

09:33.290 --> 09:34.810
All right, it hit!

09:35.280 --> 09:36.590
It is super effective.

09:40.490 --> 09:41.870
It's recovering again.

09:42.300 --> 09:44.090
At this rate, it will be the same thing all over again.

09:47.350 --> 09:47.960
Avalanche!

09:50.080 --> 09:50.600
Here it comes!

09:55.550 --> 09:56.390
Fiarrow!

10:00.640 --> 10:02.110
Are you all right, Fiarrow?

10:04.330 --> 10:05.370
What incredible power...

10:05.920 --> 10:10.850
Avalanche is a move launched with increased power if used against an opponent that has already attacked.

10:11.130 --> 10:13.360
So even if you have more speed...

10:14.140 --> 10:15.890
...Avalanche will turn it all around.

10:16.340 --> 10:17.910
Fiarrow, fly up!

10:20.460 --> 10:21.390
Stone Edge!

10:22.940 --> 10:23.530
Dodge!

10:26.780 --> 10:27.500
Well done!

10:28.010 --> 10:31.340
Satoshi cannot afford to be careless when attacking.

10:31.900 --> 10:33.740
...Lest another Avalanche comes.

10:34.310 --> 10:34.640
But...

10:35.290 --> 10:36.920
...we can't defeat it without attacking it.

10:38.150 --> 10:39.740
Fiarrow, Flame Charge!

10:44.520 --> 10:45.150
Avalanche!

10:50.000 --> 10:50.990
Fiarrow!

10:55.790 --> 10:57.270
Fiarrow is unable to battle!

10:57.640 --> 10:59.030
Therefore, Crebase wins!

11:02.390 --> 11:04.530
Crebase is strong...

11:05.860 --> 11:08.330
He's got to do something about that Avalanche.

11:08.740 --> 11:10.940
Satoshi only has one left.

11:12.790 --> 11:15.210
Fiarrow, you fought well.

11:18.040 --> 11:20.610
All right... Gekkouga, I choose you!

11:26.550 --> 11:27.400
Pokémon Quiz.

11:27.930 --> 11:29.390
The answer is... Well, you know.

11:31.160 --> 11:40.970
Coming up next:

11:31.160 --> 11:36.130
Gekkouga VS Crebase!

11:32.090 --> 11:36.760
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:36.170 --> 11:40.970
Will Satoshi get his final badge!?

11:49.160 --> 11:50.640
His last one is Gekkouga.

11:51.070 --> 11:54.570
If this tension works to Satoshi and Gekkouga's advantage...

11:55.040 --> 11:56.860
...they will be able to become Satoshi Gekkouga!

11:59.030 --> 12:01.210
Gekkouga, don't let the hail bother you!

12:02.590 --> 12:03.170
Let's go!

12:04.090 --> 12:04.600
Use Cut!

12:08.760 --> 12:09.750
Stone Edge!

12:18.970 --> 12:19.490
Oh?

12:20.050 --> 12:20.630
It's not over yet!

12:21.100 --> 12:21.990
Aerial Ace!

12:24.640 --> 12:25.540
Gyro Ball!

12:35.040 --> 12:36.180
How about this?

12:36.650 --> 12:38.810
Gekkouga, use Water Shuriken repeatedly!

12:44.890 --> 12:45.510
It's no use!

12:51.160 --> 12:52.440
I said it's no...

12:52.880 --> 12:53.050
Hm?!

12:57.610 --> 12:58.460
I-Impossible!

12:58.860 --> 12:59.780
Go!

13:00.070 --> 13:00.960
Use Cut!

13:09.700 --> 13:10.780
They did it!

13:10.780 --> 13:12.940
Citron, what's going on?

13:13.380 --> 13:18.090
The water that burst from Water Shuriken splashed onto Crebase and froze.

13:18.400 --> 13:19.170
I see.

13:19.570 --> 13:20.650
So that's why its movements were...

13:24.760 --> 13:27.850
That... What was it? That sure surprised me!

13:28.290 --> 13:29.410
Good job, Gekkouga!

13:30.030 --> 13:31.950
Let's show them our power.

13:34.640 --> 13:37.180
Stronger... Much stronger!

13:44.200 --> 13:44.960
There it is!

13:45.660 --> 13:46.830
It's Satoshi Gekkouga!

13:47.700 --> 13:48.840
"Satoshi Gekkouga"?

13:49.280 --> 13:51.780
But that is the form I have already seen before.

13:52.890 --> 13:54.000
Let's go, Gekkouga!

13:55.760 --> 13:56.920
Aerial Ace!

14:08.720 --> 14:09.220
It's fast!

14:11.150 --> 14:11.900
Avalanche!

14:20.940 --> 14:23.800
Satoshi can feel the damage Gekkouga takes?

14:24.420 --> 14:25.410
Impossible...

14:25.720 --> 14:26.340
They have become one...

14:26.780 --> 14:29.080
In other words, <i>everything</i> is synchronized.

14:29.310 --> 14:31.380
Gekkouga, Satoshi, hang in there!

14:32.080 --> 14:32.720
Satoshi...

14:35.000 --> 14:35.810
I want to win!

14:36.710 --> 14:38.520
No matter what, I want...

14:41.200 --> 14:41.990
...to win this match!

14:44.880 --> 14:46.550
Gekkouga, use Cut!

14:49.050 --> 14:49.940
Stone Edge!

15:02.080 --> 15:03.640
Use Stone Edge again!

15:10.040 --> 15:10.660
Gekkouga!

15:13.690 --> 15:14.340
I'm okay.

15:14.730 --> 15:15.640
Aerial Ace!

15:26.790 --> 15:28.990
Oh? I had no idea it had this kind of power...

15:30.510 --> 15:30.940
But...

15:31.710 --> 15:32.950
Avalanche!

15:37.440 --> 15:38.180
Gekkouga!

15:43.550 --> 15:44.020
More...

15:44.510 --> 15:45.170
More!

15:46.270 --> 15:48.070
Gekkouga, Cut!

15:52.340 --> 15:53.070
Ice Fang!

15:59.270 --> 16:00.010
Gyro Ball!

16:07.890 --> 16:08.470
Gekkouga!

16:23.070 --> 16:24.410
Gekkouga is unable to battle!

16:24.780 --> 16:26.020
Crebase wins!

16:26.560 --> 16:29.210
Therefore, the winner is Gym Leader Urup!

16:37.760 --> 16:39.530
Did I... lose...?

16:41.930 --> 16:47.680
Water can adapt to its environment without changing its essential qualities.

16:48.600 --> 16:52.950
I can't do that. That's why I love Ice types.

16:53.740 --> 16:55.450
How about you?

16:59.240 --> 17:02.930
How far you can go depends on how much you believe in your Pokémon.

17:04.360 --> 17:06.850
I can't let you have the badge yet.

17:26.910 --> 17:27.630
How is it doing?

17:28.330 --> 17:31.360
It has taken a lot of damage, both physically and mentally.

17:31.930 --> 17:32.850
But it'll be fine.

17:33.320 --> 17:33.860
Leave it to me.

17:44.400 --> 17:44.990
You're leaving?

17:45.350 --> 17:45.680
Yes.

17:46.070 --> 17:49.130
I will start preparing my Pokémon for the League.

17:51.500 --> 17:52.170
Satoshi...

17:52.910 --> 17:53.870
I will be waiting for you.

17:54.910 --> 17:55.260
Yeah.

18:01.600 --> 18:03.780
All right then, I will now excuse myself.

18:04.100 --> 18:04.720
See you!

18:06.670 --> 18:07.520
Take care.

18:11.590 --> 18:12.490
It is fine this way.

18:13.820 --> 18:14.900
The person I admire...

18:16.130 --> 18:17.340
...will definitely win.

18:19.280 --> 18:19.980
I will be waiting.

18:20.420 --> 18:21.780
I am waiting.

18:23.180 --> 18:24.560
Let us meet in a League match.

18:35.740 --> 18:37.330
I'm sorry about today, Gekkouga.

18:38.570 --> 18:40.180
If I had got my act together...

18:41.950 --> 18:44.270
...we should've been able to draw out that power of yours.

18:46.390 --> 18:47.660
If only I had got my act together...

18:54.320 --> 18:55.140
Satoshi...

19:05.270 --> 19:06.290
I want to be alone.

19:08.320 --> 19:09.800
At this hour?

19:10.510 --> 19:10.940
Don't worry.

19:11.920 --> 19:12.950
I'll be back in a minute.

19:13.850 --> 19:14.740
Pikachu, I'm sorry...

19:39.270 --> 19:41.790
In the end, he never came back.

19:42.000 --> 19:42.390
No.

19:42.910 --> 19:44.890
But right now, there is nothing we...

19:45.430 --> 19:46.330
Good morning.

19:47.510 --> 19:47.780
Huh?

19:48.320 --> 19:49.070
Where's Satoshi?

19:52.280 --> 19:53.580
I'm going out for a bit.

19:54.200 --> 19:58.150
Do not worry. By lunchtime he will be back, saying he got hungry.

20:05.430 --> 20:06.000
Satoshi...

20:10.360 --> 20:15.630
Having been defeated in his Eisetsu Gym match, Satoshi has come to the forest looking for answers.

20:16.930 --> 20:21.380
Will he be able to escape this situation?

20:29.060 --> 20:30.290
Pokémon Twenty Four Hours!

20:31.560 --> 20:35.960
All right, in today's "Pokémon Twenty Four Hours", we're going to give a detailed report on Urup-san of the Eisetsu Gym.

20:36.460 --> 20:39.560
Urup-san here uses Ice type Pokémon.

20:39.920 --> 20:44.070
He specializes in attacks that cleverly make use of the ice rink that covers the floor.

20:44.560 --> 20:49.400
Incredibly, Urup-san is thinly dressed like this throughout the year, even inside his ice cold Gym!

20:50.040 --> 20:53.080
Surely it's because he battles in such a heated manner that he doesn't feel the cold.

21:01.520 --> 21:03.170
Whoa, awesome!

21:04.550 --> 21:05.720
Aren't you cold?

21:06.460 --> 21:10.500
Well, you know. If you clear your mind, it's... You know.

21:11.390 --> 21:11.910
You know...

21:15.190 --> 21:17.090
What?!

21:17.310 --> 21:19.740
Th-That's all for Pokémon Twenty Four Hours!

21:20.970 --> 21:25.970
Sunday May 22nd at 8am!

21:22.120 --> 21:25.080
At Pokénchi, they try to replicate Pikachu's Thunder!

21:28.300 --> 21:30.220
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.390 --> 21:31.480
Towards our next adventure!

21:42.470 --> 21:45.830
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:47.940 --> 21:51.840
The Winding Woods... The Dawn of Evolution!

21:52.490 --> 21:55.980
Next Time

21:52.490 --> 21:55.980
The Winding Woods... The Dawn of Evolution!

21:56.020 --> 22:05.950
Next episode:

21:56.020 --> 22:00.960
Satoshi is in the forest, feeling lost...

21:56.890 --> 22:01.490
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:01.040 --> 22:05.950
What answer will Satoshi find there!?
